Why: the air-unit encoder must be able to change bitrate during an active
stream. The closed low-delay stack updates encoder rate control on MCS changes
without rebuilding the video pipeline; the open stack needs the same shape for
future reception-driven adaptation.

Keep the userspace API as ordinary V4L2 controls. BITRATE, VBV_SIZE and S_PARM
mark a pending live update while streaming; the encoder worker consumes that
pending state before queuing the next picture and applies the dynamic fields
through W5_ENC_SET_PARAM / OPT_CHANGE_PARAM using the same change flags as the
vendor Wave5 stack.

W5_ENC_SET_PARAM completes asynchronously and leaves one report on the instance
report queue, for OPT_CHANGE_PARAM exactly as for the OPT_COMMON sequence init.
Vendor ar_video_h26x_enc_msg_set_param_done() drains that report with
VPU_EncGetOutputInfo() before letting the encoder resume, so the change command
carries the same wait-then-GET_RESULT handshake here.

